LAMMPS (22 Jul 2025 - Update 4)
# Crowders in a box with fixed x and y boundaries and no walls; thermo_style
# one. Atoms leave the box, and the default "thermo_modify lost error" stops
# LAMMPS with an ERROR line inside the thermo table: no "Loop time of" and
# no "Total wall time".

units           lj
dimension       3
boundary        f f p
atom_style      atomic

variable        randseed equal 6121
region          box block -5 5 -5 5 -5 5 units box
create_box      1 box
Created orthogonal box = (-5 -5 -5) to (5 5 5)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
create_atoms    1 random 100 ${randseed} box overlap 1.0 maxtry 100 units box
create_atoms    1 random 100 6121 box overlap 1.0 maxtry 100 units box
Created 100 atoms
  using box units in orthogonal box = (-5 -5 -5) to (5 5 5)
  create_atoms CPU = 0.000 seconds
mass            1 1.0
pair_style      lj/cut 1.122462
pair_modify     shift yes
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 1.122462
neighbor        0.3 bin

velocity        all create 5.0 ${randseed}
velocity        all create 5.0 6121
fix             F_nve all nve/limit 0.05
thermo          100
thermo_style    one
thermo_modify   flush yes
timestep        0.005
run             5000
Generated 0 of 0 mixed pair_coeff terms from geometric mixing rule
Neighbor list info ...
  update: every = 1 steps, delay = 0 steps, check = yes
  max neighbors/atom: 2000, page size: 100000
  master list distance cutoff = 1.422462
  ghost atom cutoff = 1.422462
  binsize = 0.711231, bins = 15 15 15
  1 neighbor lists, perpetual/occasional/extra = 1 0 0
  (1) pair lj/cut, perpetual
      attributes: half, newton on
      pair build: half/bin/atomonly/newton
      stencil: half/bin/3d
      bin: standard
Per MPI rank memory allocation (min/avg/max) = 3.072 | 3.072 | 3.072 Mbytes
   Step          Temp          E_pair         E_mol          TotEng         Press     
         0   5              0.021069466    0              7.4460695      0.51923418   
ERROR: Lost atoms: original 100 current 80
